{{also|VOX|VOx}}
==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ine-pro|la}} {{m|ine-pro|*wṓkʷs||speech, voice}}, an [[o-grade]] [[root noun]] of {{m|ine-pro|*wekʷ-||to speak}}. Cognates include {{etyl|sa|-}} {{term|sc=Deva|वाच्|tr=vā́c|lang=sa}} and {{etyl|grc|-}} {{term|sc=polytonic|ὄψ|tr=óps|lang=grc}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Classical}} {{IPA|/woːks/|lang=la}}
* {{audio|la-cls-vox.ogg|Audio (Classical)|lang=la}}

===Noun===
{{la-noun|vōx|vocis#Latin|vōcis|f|third}}

# [[voice]]
# [[accent]]
# [[speech]], [[remark]]
# {{context|grammar|lang=la}} [[voice]]; indicating the relation of the subject of the verb to the action which the verb expresses
# {{inflection of|lang=la|vox||voc|s}}

